{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB 5% Annual General Adjustment cap and coverage changes","requirement":"The Rent Board's Annual General Adjustment for fully covered units is capped at 5% per year; government-owned or subsidized units become fully or partially covered and must be registered, and utility charges must be set into base rent unless separately metered.","key_value":"5% per year maximum AGA","coverage_conditions":"Fully covered units (most multifamily built before 1980, single-family homes with pre-1996 tenancies, rooms rented individually with five or more rooms) and newly covered government-owned or subsidized units. Partially covered: post-1980 new construction, most single-family homes and condominiums.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":"1980","built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Fully or partially covered units under the Berkeley Rent Ordinance; shared kitchen or bath units exempt only if the landlord resided on the same property at tenancy start"},"exemptions":"Units where the tenant shares kitchen or bath with the landlord are exempt only if the landlord lived on the same property at the start of the tenancy. Units with Section 202 or Section 811 subsidies are partially covered regardless of unit type.","penalty":"The Rent Board may impose fines for failure to report new tenancies within 15 days, but must first adopt regulations creating a fine system.","effective_date":null,"citation":"Measure BB (Nov. 2024 ballot measure amending Berkeley Rent Ordinance)","quoted_span":"The maximum AGA is 5%. This means that, if the formula in the Rent Ordinance results in an AGA that is greater than 5%, the AGA approved by the Board for that year can be no more than 5%.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB just cause eviction changes","requirement":"A landlord may not evict for rental debt under one month's Fair Market Rent or for refusing to sign a substantially similar lease; lease-breach evictions require actual harm to the landlord, and notice copies must be filed with the Rent Board within three business days.","key_value":"1 month FMR (Oakland-Fremont HUD metro)","coverage_conditions":"Tenants in units fully or partially covered by the Berkeley Rent Ordinance.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Units fully or partially covered by the Berkeley Rent Ordinance"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Measure BB (Nov. 2024 ballot measure amending Berkeley Rent Ordinance)","quoted_span":"For a landlord to evict a tenant for nonpayment of rent, the tenant must owe an amount of rental debt equal to or greater than one month of the Fair Market Rent (FMR) value for a unit of equivalent size in the metro area Oakland-Fremont, CA HUD Metro FMR as determined by the US Department of Housing and Urban Development for the fiscal year in which the rent is demanded.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
